        "original_id": "e3446614-c7cc-5374-ba54-293feb677b91",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Suho, Baekhyun, Chanyeol, D.O., Kai, Sehun, Xiumin, Lay, Chen, Kris, Luhan, Tao\n- Companies: S.M. Entertainment\n- Organizations: EXO, Exo-K, Exo-M\n- Products: \"Coming Over\"\n- Topics: Japanese single albums, South Korean boy groups\n\nFacts:\n- S.M. Entertainment formed EXO in 2011.\n- EXO debuted in 2012 with twelve members.\n- EXO was separated into the subgroups Exo-K and Exo-M at debut.\n- Exo-K consisted of Suho, Baekhyun, Chanyeol, D.O., Kai, and Sehun and performed in Korean.\n- Exo-M consisted of Xiumin, Lay, Chen, Kris, Luhan, and Tao and performed in Mandarin.\n- Kris, Luhan, and Tao were later former members of EXO.\n- \"Coming Over\" is the second Japanese single album by the South Korean boy group EXO.",
